---
title: Apple Sauce
description: Apple purée, traditionally served with roast pork
servings: 6
course: Main
prep time: 10m
cook time: 20m
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: British
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- condiment
- sauce
- savoury
- british
- vegetarian
---

Peel, core and chop the @cooking apples{4%large} into chunks.

Put the apples, @sugar{55%g}, @lemon juice{2%tbsp}, @cloves{4}, and @water{1%tbsp}, into a #saucepan. Simmer with the lid on until the apples are soft (about ~{20%minutes}).

Discard the cloves and add the @butter{55%g}.

Mash the apples with a #potato masher{} until puréed.